gather_strip — INTEGRATION SKETCH (not applied; the coordinator owns integration)
================================================================================

MEASURED CONCLUSION FIRST, because it changes the shape of the patch:

The strip form's COMPUTE-SIDE CONTRACT is "block_width_tiles = SRC_PAGE_TILES"
(the source shard's width in tiles). That is forced no matter how the reader
groups its CB pushes -- strip s of a block holds tile-columns
[s*page_tiles, (s+1)*page_tiles), so the library tilize helper has to be called
at page_tiles width over `slices` x more blocks.

Given that, "strip-major layout at the op's current WT_CHUNK" and "just set
WT_CHUNK = SRC_PAGE_TILES" differ ONLY in the reader's CB-reserve / barrier
granularity, and they MEASURE FLAT against each other:

    focus reshard [1,1,1024,256] bf16 W2 -> H8, end-to-end device kernel ns
      op today                                    19,488
      strip-major, WT_CHUNK 8, slices 2           15,365   1.27x
      WT_CHUNK 4 == page_tiles, slices 1          15,456   1.26x   <- FLAT

and their PRECONDITIONS are identical (strip needs page_tiles | WT_CHUNK, and
WT_CHUNK | SHARD_WT, hence page_tiles | SHARD_WT -- which is exactly what the
re-block needs).

So there are two integration forms. Form A is strictly simpler and buys the same
number on every W_REGION plan; Form B is only needed where the host is not free
to choose WT_CHUNK (the generic W_BLOCKS grid split, where WT_CHUNK is picked for
grid fill and pipeline depth).


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FORM A -- "coalesce the block": prefer WT_CHUNK == SRC_PAGE_TILES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NO compute-kernel change. NO writer change. NO CB-layout change. One reader
branch + one host blocking preference.

